          {
            "x": 2.178649237472767,
            "y": 12.910611231371064,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Personal Tragedies</strong><br>\nFranz Joseph's personal life was marked by tragedy, including the execution of his brother Maximilian in Mexico, the suicide of his son Crown Prince Rudolf, and the assassination of his wife, Empress Elisabeth.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Last Years and Death</strong><br>\nIn his last years, Franz Joseph became an iconic figure of a vanishing era as his health and the fortunes of his empire declined. He died on November 21, 1916, in the midst of World War I.</p>\n\n<p><strong>End of an Era</strong><br>\nFranz Joseph's death marked the end of an era for the Habsburg dynasty. His long reign witnessed the transformation of European politics and the eventual disintegration of the Austro-Hungarian Empire.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
